WEBVTT

00:00:29.038 --> 00:00:31.913
or do you go with your first impression
and write him off?

00:00:31.996 --> 00:00:34.746
Research in social psychology suggests

00:00:34.787 --> 00:00:37.496
that we’re quick to form
lasting impressions of others

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:39.579
based on their behaviors.

00:00:39.621 --> 00:00:41.537
We manage to do this with little effort,

00:00:41.579 --> 00:00:44.954
inferring stable character traits
from a single behavior,

00:00:44.996 --> 00:00:47.496
like a harsh word or a clumsy step.

00:00:47.537 --> 00:00:49.287
Using our impressions as guides,

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:51.329
we can accurately predict

00:00:51.371 --> 00:00:53.537
how people are going 
to behave in the future.

00:00:53.579 --> 00:00:55.996
Armed with the knowledge
that the football game guy

00:00:56.037 --> 00:00:58.121
was a jerk the first time you met him,

00:00:58.162 --> 00:01:00.454
you might expect more 
of the same down the road.